WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:03.148
Melanie heard the crashing dishes from the kitchen.

2
00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:05.273
"You okay out there?"

3
00:00:05.274 --> 00:00:08.939
"Everything is fine!" Ally called back.

4
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.450
"But I need those three pancake orders and two oatmeals again."

5
00:00:13.451 --> 00:00:17.502
"Got it!" Melanie said.

6
00:00:17.503 --> 00:00:21.247
Ally flushed as she scrambled to clean up the mess.

7
00:00:21.248 --> 00:00:24.197
"This is embarrassing," she thought.

8
00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:27.847
"Melanie must think I'm a terrible waitress!"

9
00:00:27.848 --> 00:00:32.238
"Let me help." Melanie came out of the kitchen with a mop.

10
00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:34.649
"I've worked in tons of restaurants.

11
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.768
Things like this happen."

12
00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.424
Tina was watching Ally.

13
00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:44.851
"Why didn't you do one of those tricks Phil told me about, Ally?"

14
00:00:44.852 --> 00:00:47.571
Ally felt tears burning in her eyes.

15
00:00:47.572 --> 00:00:51.588
"If only I could," she thought.

16
00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:58.126
"Er . . . I guess I've lost interest in doing them," Ally said.

17
00:00:58.127 --> 00:01:01.263
"I understand." Tina nodded.

18
00:01:01.264 --> 00:01:04.638
"I used to love teaching, did it for thirty years.

19
00:01:04.639 --> 00:01:12.491
But one day I woke up and thought to myself, 'Tina, you've got to pursue your space dreams!'"

20
00:01:12.492 --> 00:01:15.738
"Space dreams?" Ally repeated.

21
00:01:15.739 --> 00:01:19.254
"I love all things space," Tina said.

22
00:01:19.255 --> 00:01:25.264
"I'm too old now to become an astronaut, but I'm not too old to do lots of other things.

23
00:01:25.265 --> 00:01:32.163
So I decided to move to the home of the Sandville UFO Museum.

24
00:01:32.164 --> 00:01:36.230
I couldn't believe my luck when I got a job at the museum!

25
00:01:36.231 --> 00:01:43.263
Like I told my son, if I can't go to space, at least I can work close to it."

26
00:01:43.264 --> 00:01:49.430
"Ally almost went to space," Phil said. "With the billionaire Lainie Polk."

27
00:01:49.431 --> 00:01:55.005
"Almost," Ally said. "She canceled the trip."

28
00:01:55.006 --> 00:01:57.100
"I know," Tina said.

29
00:01:57.101 --> 00:02:00.360
"I was so disappointed when that happened.

30
00:02:00.361 --> 00:02:02.820
I was going to track that flight.

31
00:02:02.821 --> 00:02:07.973
But I didn't realize until now—that was you!"

32
00:02:07.974 --> 00:02:14.244
Tina was bringing up all kinds of things Ally didn't want to talk or think about.

33
00:02:14.245 --> 00:02:17.824
Ally put down the broom and wiped her hands on her apron.

34
00:02:17.825 --> 00:02:21.784
"Excuse me, I'm going to the restroom."

35
00:02:21.785 --> 00:02:25.423
"Hurry back," Tina said with a grin.

36
00:02:25.424 --> 00:02:31.170
"I'll tell you about the article I was just reading about Lainie Polk's latest project.

37
00:02:31.171 --> 00:02:35.088
She's creating a sanctuary for penguins."

38
00:02:35.089 --> 00:02:39.066
"Okay," Ally said.

39
00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:42.603
But she didn't want to hear anything about Lainie Polk either.

40
00:02:42.604 --> 00:02:53.949
If Lainie hadn't changed her mind about going to space, Ally would still have her powers, and she'd be home on Astralia by now.

41
00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:57.293
At the end of the shift, Ally was getting ready to go home.

42
00:02:57.294 --> 00:03:03.572
"Finally, I can get back to Alpha and see what she has to say about Patagonia," she thought, heading for the door.

43
00:03:03.573 --> 00:03:08.920
"Wait, don't leave yet, Ally!" Melanie called as she came out of the kitchen.

44
00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:14.025
"You did such a great job today handling the shift on your own, I made you a special treat."

45
00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:19.056
Melanie handed Ally a glass filled with a bright green smoothie.

46
00:03:19.057 --> 00:03:24.926
"This is my secret recipe, I developed it . . . a long way from here."

47
00:03:24.927 --> 00:03:30.104
Ally looked at the smoothie. "Strange," she thought.

48
00:03:30.105 --> 00:03:39.089
The color, the texture, even the smell, reminded her of one of her favorite treats back home, a Galorpian astroshake.

49
00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:43.049
Ally took a sip, and then another one.

50
00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:48.904
"Wow! This even tastes just like a Galorp—" Ally caught herself.

51
00:03:48.905 --> 00:03:51.062
"A glorious treat!"

52
00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:56.543
Melanie smiled. "I had a suspicion you might like it."

53
00:03:56.544 --> 00:04:01.934
"You did?" Ally narrowed her eyes. "Why is that?"

54
00:04:01.935 --> 00:04:06.068
"You look like someone with exotic taste."

55
00:04:06.069 --> 00:04:09.347
Melanie held up the blender. "Want more?"

56
00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:17.486
"Uh, sure." Ally wanted to taste it again to convince herself that there was no way it could be a Galorpian astroshake.

57
00:04:17.487 --> 00:04:21.254
Ally tipped her head back and drank up the entire glass.

58
00:04:21.255 --> 00:04:25.504
"It sure tastes like an astroshake," she thought.

59
00:04:25.505 --> 00:04:31.593
She was about to ask about the ingredients when Melanie pointed to Ally's meld medallion.

60
00:04:31.594 --> 00:04:35.579
"That's a nice charm. I have something similar."

61
00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:40.130
"What?" Ally thought, nearly dropping the glass she was holding.

62
00:04:40.131 --> 00:04:43.649
First, Melanie had made the Galorpian astroshake.

63
00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:48.351
Now she was revealing that she also had a meld medallion.

64
00:04:48.352 --> 00:04:51.927
Was there a chance that Melanie was an alien life-form too?

65
00:04:51.928 --> 00:04:55.158
Or could she just be testing Ally for some reason?

66
00:04:55.159 --> 00:05:03.296
Before Ally had a chance to sort out the thoughts whirling through her head, Melanie was grabbing her backpack and heading for the door.

67
00:05:03.297 --> 00:05:07.704
"Glad you liked the shake, Ally. You'll lock up the diner, right?"

68
00:05:07.705 --> 00:05:10.775
"Uh, yeah," Ally muttered.

69
00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:18.244
"See you tomorrow!" And with that Melanie was gone.

70
00:05:18.245 --> 00:05:23.721
In a daze, Ally turned off the lights.

71
00:05:23.722 --> 00:05:27.880
"I've got to get home quickly for another reason now," she thought.

72
00:05:27.881 --> 00:05:33.930
"I need Alpha to scan Sandville to see if there are any other alien life-forms in town!"

